  "199 runners raced on foot across America.",
  "In 1928, they set off from Los Angeles for New York.",
  "It was a stunt to promote the brand-new Route 66.",
  "That's about 3,400 miles in 84 days.",
  "Newspapers called it the Bunion Derby, and only 55 finished.",
  "The winner was Andy Payne, a Cherokee farm kid from Oklahoma.",
  "His $25,000 prize paid off his family's farm.",
  "But the promoter still lost money, after..."
